WEBVTT

01:41.860 --> 01:48.950
[Genius Girlfriend]

01:49.620 --> 01:51.800
[Episode 4]

02:02.480 --> 02:04.200
Morning, Angel's Tears.

02:04.950 --> 02:06.920
Morning, Scythe.

02:08.360 --> 02:09.680
Still a fan of Han Geng?

02:09.910 --> 02:11.680
If you ask me, you should be my fan.

02:11.680 --> 02:14.140
I look so handsome
when playing basketball.

02:14.310 --> 02:16.150
Don't even bring it up.
Just thinking about it ticks me off.

02:16.150 --> 02:18.150
My mom doesn't even
let me go online anymore.

02:18.150 --> 02:19.430
I've had it good these past few days.

02:19.430 --> 02:20.750
My dad's over the moon,

02:20.800 --> 02:23.120
all because I'm entering the math contest.

02:23.120 --> 02:24.120
The math contest?

02:24.150 --> 02:25.680
Who are you teaming up with?

02:25.680 --> 02:27.210
Lin Zhixia and Shen Fuxuan.

02:28.590 --> 02:29.470
Lin Zhixia?

02:29.840 --> 02:32.310
Then I'd rather never go online
for the rest of my life.

02:32.310 --> 02:33.800
You're dead last in the class.

02:33.800 --> 02:34.910
Even if you wanted to join,

02:34.910 --> 02:36.970
you'd need a team willing to take you.

02:37.120 --> 02:37.840
I...

02:40.079 --> 02:40.710
Get lost.

02:42.120 --> 02:42.960
Fine, I'll go.

02:43.590 --> 02:45.390
Make sure you don't show up late.

02:47.190 --> 02:48.120
Wait for me!

02:53.680 --> 02:55.240
The contest is only 10 days away.

02:55.240 --> 02:57.079
Based on each of our strengths and needs,

02:57.079 --> 02:58.360
I've put together a study plan.

02:58.360 --> 02:59.150
Take a look.

02:59.960 --> 03:01.000
Okay.

03:02.120 --> 03:04.210
If we finish this plan before the contest,

03:04.210 --> 03:05.740
we should be in good shape.

03:07.060 --> 03:08.090
Take a look and see
if there's anything else

03:08.090 --> 03:09.750
you think needs improvement.

03:10.360 --> 03:11.150
Lin Zhixia,

03:11.870 --> 03:13.530
this is 10 days' worth of work?

03:17.630 --> 03:19.030
I have no problem with it.

03:29.470 --> 03:30.280
Okay.

03:30.870 --> 03:31.680
Okay.

03:32.360 --> 03:33.240
Then let's get our things together

03:33.240 --> 03:34.240
and meet at the library.

03:34.240 --> 03:34.840
Okay.

03:37.910 --> 03:39.360
I'm going to the restroom.

03:39.360 --> 03:41.020
I'll catch up with you in a bit.

03:45.730 --> 03:48.300
[A New Chapter, A New Journey]

03:52.840 --> 03:54.870
I've got a problem.

03:56.960 --> 04:00.290
Had I known it'd be this exhausting,
I wouldn't have joined.

04:07.120 --> 04:07.910
Duan Qiyan,

04:08.150 --> 04:09.610
let me see your study plan.

04:15.520 --> 04:19.290
[A New Chapter, A New Journey]

04:16.870 --> 04:18.040
I can't show it to you.

04:18.040 --> 04:19.390
Aren't you our competitor?

04:19.390 --> 04:21.120
It's classified information.

04:21.560 --> 04:23.890
[A New Chapter, A New Journey]

04:32.680 --> 04:33.360
Alright.

04:33.480 --> 04:34.830
That's it for now.

04:34.070 --> 04:36.540
[Please Keep Quiet in the Library]

04:35.480 --> 04:37.140
We'll continue after school.

04:37.830 --> 04:38.220
Okay.

04:38.390 --> 04:40.320
We'll still be going after school?

04:40.480 --> 04:42.810
Isn't today's workload a little too much?

04:42.870 --> 04:44.670
Didn't you look at the schedule?

04:44.830 --> 04:46.560
Why are you still complaining?

04:47.190 --> 04:49.430
Actually, your fundamentals aren't bad.

04:49.430 --> 04:51.850
Once you get used to
contest-style thinking,

04:51.850 --> 04:53.659
it won't just help you in this contest—

04:53.659 --> 04:56.260
it'll help with your studies
in the future too.

04:57.000 --> 04:57.860
I don't know...

05:50.570 --> 05:51.250
Duan Qiyan.

05:53.220 --> 05:54.950
How's your contest prep going?

05:57.220 --> 05:59.100
This is no way to live.

06:00.890 --> 06:01.930
I've got an idea

06:01.930 --> 06:04.190
that'll make things a lot easier for you.

06:09.100 --> 06:10.300
Tell me more about it.

06:10.810 --> 06:12.810
From what I saw of Lin Zhixia's plan,

06:12.890 --> 06:13.620
her focus

06:13.620 --> 06:15.540
is on developing your overall ability.

06:15.540 --> 06:18.300
She wants to turn both of you
into versions of herself.

06:18.300 --> 06:20.500
However, we want each person
to play to their strengths

06:20.500 --> 06:21.890
and work together as a team.

06:21.890 --> 06:22.690
You wouldn't need to study

06:22.690 --> 06:24.290
all that advanced material—

06:24.330 --> 06:27.190
just what's needed
for this contest specifically.

06:27.620 --> 06:29.540
So, do you want to join our team?

06:37.750 --> 06:42.409
[Registration Form]

06:40.330 --> 06:41.420
Why is Duan Qiyan's name

06:41.420 --> 06:42.680
on both of these forms?

06:53.490 --> 06:54.700
[Registration Form]

06:58.070 --> 06:58.870
Ms. Wu,

06:59.240 --> 07:01.500
why don't we just ask Duan Qiyan himself?

07:07.390 --> 07:08.650
I'm sorry, Lin Zhixia.

07:09.480 --> 07:12.080
I think I'd be a better fit
on Jin Baihui's team.

07:12.430 --> 07:13.430
I was actually planning

07:13.430 --> 07:14.800
to tell you guys about this today.

07:14.800 --> 07:15.560
But I didn't expect

07:15.560 --> 07:18.390
the registration forms
to reach the teacher so fast.

07:18.390 --> 07:20.590
Didn't you already promise Lin Zhixia?

07:21.830 --> 07:22.600
You don't know.

07:22.600 --> 07:24.680
Their training is way too intense.

07:24.830 --> 07:26.830
I'm afraid I won't be able to keep up.

07:28.630 --> 07:30.240
Didn't we agree on this before?

07:30.240 --> 07:31.700
How can you be so disloyal?

07:32.100 --> 07:32.600
Well...

07:33.480 --> 07:35.270
This has nothing to do with loyalty.

07:35.270 --> 07:36.000
Before registration closes,

07:36.000 --> 07:37.820
every contestant has the right
to choose whichever team they want.

07:37.820 --> 07:38.820
That's not wrong.

07:51.430 --> 07:53.159
Alright, that's settled then.

07:53.480 --> 07:55.040
There are only 2 days left
until registration closes.

07:55.040 --> 07:56.840
Hurry up and find a new teammate.

08:18.070 --> 08:19.430
That traitor Duan Qiyan,

08:19.430 --> 08:20.510
so unreliable.

08:22.160 --> 08:24.680
There are only 2 days left
until registration closes.

08:24.680 --> 08:26.430
Where are we supposed to find someone now?

08:26.430 --> 08:27.240
It's okay.

08:27.870 --> 08:29.000
We'll find someone.

08:36.120 --> 08:36.909
Duan Qiyan,

08:37.440 --> 08:39.840
that was seriously lacking in team spirit.

08:40.440 --> 08:41.789
I invited him.

08:43.890 --> 08:44.700
Jiang Yubai,

08:45.670 --> 08:47.800
do you think I'm targeting Lin Zhixia?

08:50.440 --> 08:51.240
You're wrong.

08:51.240 --> 08:53.200
I am helping you—helping our team.

08:54.480 --> 08:56.120
You only care about defeating Lin Zhixia.

08:56.120 --> 08:57.360
But this is a team competition,

08:57.360 --> 08:58.690
not your personal show.

08:59.670 --> 09:00.550
But he is Lin Zhixia's

09:00.550 --> 09:01.960
hard-won teammate.

09:02.790 --> 09:03.960
Duan Qiyan is a person,

09:03.960 --> 09:05.080
not some object.

09:05.480 --> 09:07.360
If he genuinely wanted to
stay on their team,

09:07.360 --> 09:09.690
could I have still
gotten him to join ours?

09:13.480 --> 09:14.270
Besides,

09:14.630 --> 09:16.490
we didn't have a full team before,

09:16.670 --> 09:18.200
and Duan Qiyan is a good fit.

09:18.390 --> 09:19.630
Math modeling contest problems

09:19.630 --> 09:21.360
often involve real-world scenarios.

09:21.360 --> 09:22.600
Duan Qiyan is good at physics.

09:22.600 --> 09:24.750
He can quickly identify
the physical principles behind a problem,

09:24.750 --> 09:28.600
helping us avoid going down
unnecessary mathematical rabbit holes.

09:28.600 --> 09:31.000
Isn't the whole point of the contest
to win?

09:31.200 --> 09:34.000
So who exactly is the one
lacking team spirit here?

09:36.270 --> 09:37.080
I'm sorry.

09:37.860 --> 09:40.460
I let my personal feelings
affect the contest.

09:41.150 --> 09:42.880
But originally, I thought that

09:43.030 --> 09:44.770
if we needed to find a teammate,

09:45.440 --> 09:47.970
it'd be much easier for us
than for Lin Zhixia.

09:48.320 --> 09:49.120
That's true.

09:50.150 --> 09:51.670
Even someone as easygoing as me

09:51.670 --> 09:52.840
has already come to your team.

09:52.840 --> 09:55.360
I figured no one would dare join hers.

09:55.790 --> 09:57.670
Could you just talk a little less?

10:15.790 --> 10:16.510
Let's go.

10:23.080 --> 10:24.870
Attention, students.

10:25.630 --> 10:26.440
This week,

10:26.670 --> 10:29.320
the school will provide
centralized training for those registered

10:29.320 --> 10:30.960
for the Star of Hope Math Contest

10:30.960 --> 10:33.790
to improve your chances
of passing the preliminary round.

10:33.790 --> 10:35.120
There will also be teams

10:35.360 --> 10:38.000
from other schools
competing in the preliminary round.

10:38.000 --> 10:40.320
Students, we cannot let our guard down.

10:41.150 --> 10:42.680
The competition is fierce,

10:42.910 --> 10:45.030
and the elimination rate is high.

10:47.440 --> 10:49.910
During the training, the teachers
will move quickly through the lessons,

10:49.910 --> 10:51.270
and there will be a lot of assignments.

10:51.270 --> 10:53.670
Your academic workload will be very heavy.

10:54.390 --> 10:57.000
The lecture hall
will stay open every day at noon,

10:57.000 --> 10:59.030
so you can come here to rest.

10:57.900 --> 11:03.540
[Lin Zhixia; Shen Fuxuan]

10:59.550 --> 11:01.480
Let's push through this together.

11:03.720 --> 11:05.600
And let's aim for good results.

11:06.320 --> 11:08.200
Are you confident you can do this?

11:08.550 --> 11:09.320
-Yes.
-Yes.

11:09.670 --> 11:10.270
Good.

11:10.690 --> 11:14.340
[Study Plan: Day 1]

11:14.410 --> 11:15.720
[Past Exam Practice] [Review of Mistakes]

11:19.130 --> 11:19.770
Here.

11:24.960 --> 11:27.200
Forget about finding a teammate for now.

11:27.200 --> 11:29.800
Want to solve a math problem
to clear your head?

11:30.480 --> 11:31.550
What math problem?

11:33.440 --> 11:34.240
One day,

11:34.630 --> 11:36.870
a triangle, a circle, and a square

11:36.910 --> 11:38.510
made plans to go shopping together.

11:38.510 --> 11:40.770
The square and the circle both showed up.

11:40.910 --> 11:42.720
What is this situation called?

11:44.670 --> 11:45.930
This is a math problem?

11:50.840 --> 11:52.120
I honestly don't know.

11:53.200 --> 11:54.930
What is this situation called?

11:56.670 --> 11:58.070
This situation is called

11:58.960 --> 12:05.420
"a congruent triangle."
(Chinese pun: "congruent triangle" sounds like "everyone’s waiting for the triangle.")

12:11.240 --> 12:12.030
Not funny?

12:13.360 --> 12:14.150
It is funny.

12:14.790 --> 12:15.850
You're hilarious.

12:21.510 --> 12:23.840
I know you're trying to comfort me.

12:24.510 --> 12:26.270
If only Duan Qiyan hadn't left.

12:26.720 --> 12:28.320
The preliminary round is about to start.

12:28.320 --> 12:29.910
Those who plan to participate

12:29.910 --> 12:31.150
already have a team.

12:31.150 --> 12:33.410
It's really not easy to find someone now.

12:37.120 --> 12:38.050
Let's eat first.

12:45.480 --> 12:46.750
It wasn't me.

12:46.750 --> 12:48.120
If it wasn't you, then who was it?

12:48.120 --> 12:49.270
The cabinet door opened by itself?

12:49.270 --> 12:50.440
I don't know either.

12:50.550 --> 12:52.030
It was like this when I came back.

12:52.030 --> 12:52.750
Come on,

12:52.870 --> 12:54.550
if you did it, just own up to it.

12:54.720 --> 12:55.960
I'm telling the truth.

12:55.960 --> 12:57.000
It wasn't me.

12:57.000 --> 12:58.870
Then how come he saw you here?

12:58.870 --> 12:59.550
Who?

12:59.550 --> 13:00.320
Him!

13:01.200 --> 13:02.630
You believe everything he says?

13:02.630 --> 13:04.080
What are you, his lackey?

13:04.200 --> 13:05.790
What's that supposed to mean?

13:05.790 --> 13:06.550
What do I mean?

13:06.550 --> 13:07.630
I'm just stating facts.
What's wrong with that?

13:07.630 --> 13:08.240
You got a problem with that?

13:08.240 --> 13:09.120
He was stating the facts too.

13:09.120 --> 13:10.200
You were right here.

13:10.200 --> 13:12.670
-Didn't I make myself clear?
-What happened?

13:12.670 --> 13:15.200
They said Mr. Wang locked
the test papers for the first round

13:15.200 --> 13:16.120
and the answer keys

13:16.120 --> 13:17.650
inside the podium cabinet.

13:17.750 --> 13:19.880
Someone picked the lock at noon today.

13:20.440 --> 13:21.440
Not "someone."

13:21.670 --> 13:23.120
It was Duan Qiyan.

13:23.200 --> 13:24.910
Right, it was him.

13:25.080 --> 13:27.440
While everyone else was
taking their lunch break,

13:27.440 --> 13:29.570
he came here alone and picked the lock.

13:30.270 --> 13:32.360
You say you weren't trying to
steal the answer keys, right?

13:32.360 --> 13:33.790
Then at 12:30 PM,

13:34.000 --> 13:35.510
when everyone had gone to eat,

13:35.510 --> 13:36.910
why did you come here by yourself?

13:36.910 --> 13:38.200
Were you really that busy?

13:38.200 --> 13:39.960
It's because I brought a USB drive

13:39.960 --> 13:42.860
and wanted to copy
the teachers' slides to take home.

13:42.860 --> 13:44.650
The computer was in the drawer,
still plugged in.

13:44.650 --> 13:46.440
Where else was I supposed to do it
but at the podium?

13:46.440 --> 13:47.480
Who can prove it?

13:48.080 --> 13:48.610
Exactly.

13:49.080 --> 13:50.540
Who among you can prove it?

13:52.080 --> 13:53.270
This is the teammate
you went to such great lengths

13:53.270 --> 13:54.200
to recruit.

13:54.840 --> 13:57.770
Shouldn't you show some team spirit
and help him out?

14:01.000 --> 14:02.750
But Duan Qiyan's grades

14:02.800 --> 14:04.530
are better than most people's.

14:05.050 --> 14:06.490
Why would he steal the answer keys?

14:06.490 --> 14:07.080
Exactly.

14:07.440 --> 14:08.960
Did you hear that?

14:09.010 --> 14:10.530
Why would I need to steal the answer keys?

14:10.530 --> 14:12.410
You're out playing basketball
every single day.

14:12.410 --> 14:13.740
You know better than anyone

14:13.740 --> 14:15.170
where you actually stand academically.

14:15.170 --> 14:16.500
If you didn't steal the answer keys,

14:16.500 --> 14:18.700
how else could your grades be this good?

14:21.050 --> 14:23.580
Duan Qiyan, can I take a look
at your USB drive?

14:38.580 --> 14:39.960
When you were copying the files,

14:39.960 --> 14:41.390
was the cabinet still intact?

14:41.390 --> 14:43.390
Yes. I remember that very clearly,

14:43.700 --> 14:45.510
because I started copying the files

14:45.510 --> 14:46.570
at around 12:30 PM.

14:46.650 --> 14:48.250
It only took about 2 minutes.

14:49.030 --> 14:52.230
The more details you give,
the more suspicious you sound.

14:52.840 --> 14:56.170
You didn't just memorize
the exact time on purpose, did you?

14:56.790 --> 14:58.630
Kuang Geng, what are you implying?

14:58.630 --> 15:02.120
-You don't know what I mean?
-What do you mean? Wanna pick a fight?

15:02.120 --> 15:03.650
Isn't he just trying to stir up trouble?

15:03.650 --> 15:06.180
When was the cabinet
discovered to be broken?

15:06.250 --> 15:07.410
And who found it?

15:07.530 --> 15:08.370
I found it.

15:08.700 --> 15:10.170
I'd just finished lunch,

15:10.220 --> 15:11.580
around 12:50 PM,

15:11.980 --> 15:14.980
and when I came in,
the door was already open like that.

15:15.460 --> 15:16.890
After copying the files,

15:16.940 --> 15:18.820
I went to the cafeteria
to grab a chicken burger

15:18.820 --> 15:20.530
and planned to bring it back here to eat.

15:20.530 --> 15:21.500
You and I—

15:21.530 --> 15:23.590
we went back here one after the other.

15:23.700 --> 15:25.460
How could it possibly have been me?

15:25.460 --> 15:27.580
I was napping in this classroom
the whole time.

15:27.580 --> 15:29.170
No one came in during that period—

15:29.170 --> 15:29.940
only you.

15:30.770 --> 15:32.830
You were napping here the whole time?

15:33.170 --> 15:33.980
Yeah.

15:34.320 --> 15:35.360
In that case...

15:36.700 --> 15:38.360
there are very few witnesses.

15:39.960 --> 15:41.490
Your statement is crucial.

15:41.770 --> 15:44.300
You need to think carefully
before you speak.

15:45.750 --> 15:47.320
A real man owns up to what he does.

15:47.320 --> 15:48.700
If I'd done this, I'd definitely admit it.

15:48.700 --> 15:49.750
But I really didn't do it.

15:49.750 --> 15:51.410
Quit making things up about me.

15:51.410 --> 15:52.070
Who's making things up?

15:52.070 --> 15:52.850
Who's making things up?

15:52.850 --> 15:54.120
-How are we making anything up?
-I said you two.

15:54.120 --> 15:55.120
I haven't even...

16:03.250 --> 16:04.310
What are you doing?

16:04.870 --> 16:05.800
Starting a riot?

16:14.940 --> 16:16.270
Who opened the cabinet?

16:17.370 --> 16:18.170
Sir,

16:18.810 --> 16:19.350
he did.

16:19.770 --> 16:22.300
Seriously, Liu Su?
Are you ever going to stop?

16:29.700 --> 16:30.960
Hey, you dropped this.

16:32.110 --> 16:33.010
It's not mine.

16:34.690 --> 16:36.250
If I'd really picked that lock,

16:36.250 --> 16:37.500
I'd have taken the exam papers out

16:37.500 --> 16:38.250
and smashed you over the head with them—

16:38.250 --> 16:39.690
then you'd finally come in first place!

16:39.690 --> 16:40.530
Smash me then!

16:40.860 --> 16:42.890
Stop it! Both of you!

16:43.340 --> 16:45.860
Mr. Wang, Duan Qiyan is innocent.

16:47.050 --> 16:48.100
I checked the timestamp

16:48.100 --> 16:49.700
of the files on his USB drive.

16:50.100 --> 16:52.370
They were transferred at exactly 12:37 PM.

16:52.370 --> 16:53.580
What does that prove?

16:53.820 --> 16:55.420
He could've copied the files

16:55.530 --> 16:56.880
and looked at the answer keys
at the same time.

16:56.880 --> 16:57.960
Besides,

16:57.980 --> 16:59.510
Kuang Geng already saw him.

16:59.750 --> 17:01.210
Let's make an assumption.

17:01.670 --> 17:03.440
If you were Duan Qiyan,

17:04.109 --> 17:06.710
what would you do first—
look at the answer keys

17:06.920 --> 17:08.270
or copy the files?

17:10.510 --> 17:11.839
If it were me,

17:12.069 --> 17:14.069
I'd take advantage of the empty room

17:14.200 --> 17:16.000
and read through the answer keys first.

17:16.000 --> 17:16.829
That way,

17:17.069 --> 17:20.000
I'd also copy the files afterward
to cover my tracks.

17:20.069 --> 17:21.000
Right now, there are files

17:21.000 --> 17:22.460
on Duan Qiyan's USB drive.

17:22.589 --> 17:24.310
If he really were the culprit,

17:24.310 --> 17:26.310
that would mean
he would've already calmly read

17:26.310 --> 17:27.400
the answer keys in secret,

17:27.400 --> 17:29.930
then covered his tracks
by copying the files.

17:30.270 --> 17:31.720
But the actual scene right now

17:31.720 --> 17:33.200
looks like a complete mess—

17:33.200 --> 17:34.720
which shows that the culprit

17:34.720 --> 17:36.400
fled in a panic.

17:36.720 --> 17:38.380
Duan Qiyan isn't the culprit.

17:38.550 --> 17:39.350
Impossible.

17:39.830 --> 17:41.030
That whole analysis of yours

17:41.030 --> 17:42.510
is just speculation.

17:43.200 --> 17:44.110
Kuang Geng,

17:44.310 --> 17:46.830
I remember you said
that during the lunch break,

17:46.830 --> 17:49.200
only Duan Qiyan came back, right?

17:49.740 --> 17:50.530
Right.

17:51.740 --> 17:53.940
Then this problem becomes very simple.

17:54.090 --> 17:55.890
If Duan Qiyan isn't the culprit,

17:56.940 --> 17:58.670
then it must be you, Kuang Geng.

17:58.900 --> 18:01.080
You're slandering me
with baseless accusations!

18:01.080 --> 18:02.770
I was napping at the time.

18:03.030 --> 18:04.900
Maybe someone else came in...

18:05.010 --> 18:06.430
At noon today,

18:06.490 --> 18:07.900
I saw a paper clip

18:07.900 --> 18:09.450
fall out of your pants pocket.

18:09.450 --> 18:10.610
I picked it up and gave it back to you,

18:10.610 --> 18:11.970
but you denied it was yours.

18:11.970 --> 18:13.970
I thought it was strange at the time—

18:14.050 --> 18:15.420
why did you refuse to admit

18:15.420 --> 18:16.370
it was yours?

18:18.310 --> 18:20.110
Let's make another assumption.

18:20.110 --> 18:23.180
Before lunch today, Kuang Geng had already

18:23.310 --> 18:25.480
planned to use a paper clip
to pick the lock

18:25.480 --> 18:26.940
and steal the answer keys.

18:27.590 --> 18:29.480
Finally, lunch break arrived.

18:29.550 --> 18:31.240
Everyone left the classroom,

18:31.310 --> 18:32.960
and you got your chance.

18:34.160 --> 18:35.560
But at that exact moment,

18:36.160 --> 18:37.360
Duan Qiyan came back.

18:41.640 --> 18:43.640
So you could only pretend to nap.

18:44.000 --> 18:45.590
After Duan Qiyan left,

18:45.830 --> 18:48.310
you took out the paper clip
you'd prepared beforehand,

18:48.310 --> 18:51.440
picked the lock,
and started looking at the answer keys.

18:55.510 --> 18:56.400
Halfway through,

18:56.400 --> 18:58.960
you heard the sound of students
coming back toward the classroom,

18:58.960 --> 19:01.680
so you hastily put the answer keys back.

19:02.380 --> 19:03.700
Whatever the result,

19:03.770 --> 19:05.270
let's leave it in fate's hands.

19:05.270 --> 19:07.200
You fled in a rush
without even having time

19:07.200 --> 19:08.550
to clean up the scene.

19:09.070 --> 19:10.270
Another assumption?

19:10.350 --> 19:11.790
How do you come up with so much nonsense?

19:11.790 --> 19:12.880
I'm warning you—

19:13.030 --> 19:15.110
without solid evidence, you should also

19:15.110 --> 19:16.770
be careful about what you say.

19:17.110 --> 19:18.750
The lock cylinder has diagonal scratches,

19:18.750 --> 19:21.000
deeper on the left
and shallower on the right,

19:21.000 --> 19:23.260
which shows the culprit is left-handed.

19:24.070 --> 19:25.330
And in this classroom,

19:26.200 --> 19:28.000
only Kuang Geng is left-handed.

19:28.880 --> 19:30.080
How did you know that?

19:30.800 --> 19:32.510
Everyone, you can check the positions

19:32.510 --> 19:34.640
of the books and water cups on the desks.

19:34.640 --> 19:36.160
Everyone else has theirs placed
on the right;

19:36.160 --> 19:38.110
only Kuang Geng has his on the left.

19:39.000 --> 19:41.200
Also, because we write frequently,

19:41.350 --> 19:42.920
we wear our watches

19:43.030 --> 19:44.880
on our non-dominant wrist.

19:45.440 --> 19:47.900
Everyone, you can check
Kuang Geng's watch.

19:48.270 --> 19:50.200
He's wearing it on his right wrist.

19:54.590 --> 19:55.960
I also noticed just now

19:56.030 --> 19:58.110
that there's a tiny blue mark
on the lock cylinder.

19:58.110 --> 20:01.240
It should be from the coating
on the paper clip peeling off.

20:01.240 --> 20:02.750
Given how little time you had,

20:02.750 --> 20:05.750
you probably weren't able to
get rid of the paper clip.

20:05.750 --> 20:06.780
So I guess

20:06.830 --> 20:08.480
the paper clip you used to pick the lock

20:08.480 --> 20:09.810
is still in your pocket.

20:19.400 --> 20:20.640
Mr. Wang, look.

20:31.550 --> 20:32.350
Zhixia,

20:32.880 --> 20:35.790
you stayed calm earlier,
thought things through logically,

20:35.790 --> 20:37.880
and exposed the person
who was really cheating.

20:37.880 --> 20:39.140
That deserves praise.

20:41.200 --> 20:43.930
However, I still have to
call you out on one thing:

20:44.000 --> 20:45.660
you were a bit reckless today.

20:47.880 --> 20:48.680
Why?

20:50.590 --> 20:52.720
You're all in adolescence now.

20:53.200 --> 20:55.680
Pride and dignity
matter more than anything.

20:55.680 --> 20:57.070
By exposing him in front of everyone,

20:57.070 --> 20:59.600
you've basically
made an enemy, understand?

21:02.510 --> 21:03.400
I understand.

21:03.920 --> 21:06.070
But they were falsely accusing Duan Qiyan
at the time.

21:06.070 --> 21:06.920
The situation was urgent,

21:06.920 --> 21:08.380
so I didn't think that far.

21:08.480 --> 21:09.280
I understand.

21:10.640 --> 21:12.700
If something similar happens again,

21:13.070 --> 21:14.870
tell the teacher your reasoning

21:15.030 --> 21:16.690
and let the teacher handle it.

21:17.960 --> 21:20.760
I'm just worried
he might try to get revenge on you.

21:20.830 --> 21:23.090
You're a girl. Who will protect you then?

21:24.030 --> 21:24.640
-Me.
-Me.

21:40.960 --> 21:41.680
And me!

21:42.200 --> 21:43.440
From today on,

21:43.440 --> 21:46.720
I, Duan Qiyan, swear to protect
Lin Zhixia with my life.

21:58.240 --> 21:59.830
Isn't it a little over the top
for the three of you

21:59.830 --> 22:01.230
to walk me home like this?

22:02.160 --> 22:03.070
Not at all.

22:03.160 --> 22:04.510
It's what I should do.

22:05.070 --> 22:07.920
Zhixia, not only did you help me
find my sports player cards,

22:07.920 --> 22:09.830
but you also defended my innocence.

22:09.830 --> 22:12.440
I owe you my life for this.

22:12.640 --> 22:13.750
So, Zhixia,

22:13.750 --> 22:15.790
if you ever need any help in the future,

22:15.790 --> 22:16.990
tell me immediately.

22:17.590 --> 22:18.560
Duan Qiyan,

22:18.590 --> 22:20.270
your attitude sure did a 180.

22:21.400 --> 22:22.530
You have some nerve saying that.

22:22.530 --> 22:23.790
If it weren't for you,

22:23.910 --> 22:25.910
would she have had all this trouble?

22:33.480 --> 22:34.200
Zhixia,

22:34.960 --> 22:37.290
I know
your team is still missing a member.

22:37.960 --> 22:39.880
But I've already submitted
my contest registration form.

22:39.880 --> 22:41.680
Trying to go back to your team now

22:41.830 --> 22:43.360
probably isn't realistic.

22:46.240 --> 22:48.700
But if I really can't
find another teammate,

22:49.000 --> 22:50.930
I might not be able to participate.

22:56.200 --> 22:57.460
I have someone in mind.

22:58.770 --> 22:59.290
Who?

23:00.850 --> 23:03.440
Mom, don't force me to participate

23:03.440 --> 23:05.000
just because Duan Qiyan signed up.

23:05.000 --> 23:07.000
His grades are way better than mine.

23:07.000 --> 23:08.640
Wouldn't it be ridiculous
for someone with my math scores

23:08.640 --> 23:09.970
to enter a math contest?

23:11.610 --> 23:13.010
I've noticed something.

23:13.640 --> 23:16.270
You're absolutely
the biggest backtalker in this house.

23:16.270 --> 23:17.070
Every time I say anything,

23:17.070 --> 23:19.070
you've always got a comeback ready.

23:19.400 --> 23:20.920
I'm your mother.

23:21.000 --> 23:22.510
Isn't this all for your own good?

23:22.510 --> 23:23.680
Then why is it

23:23.680 --> 23:25.030
that other kids have all signed up,

23:25.030 --> 23:26.400
but my kid can't?

23:26.480 --> 23:27.960
What other kids?

23:28.110 --> 23:30.440
Isn't it just Lin Zhixia
who has signed up?

23:30.590 --> 23:31.720
She's the top student in the whole school.

23:31.720 --> 23:33.400
If she doesn't participate, who will?

23:33.400 --> 23:35.000
Hardly anyone
from other classes signed up.

23:35.000 --> 23:37.240
Why do you have to compare yourself
to students from other classes?

23:37.240 --> 23:39.750
Can't you just
compare yourself with Lin Zhixia?

23:39.750 --> 23:41.960
If you must compare me to Lin Zhixia,

23:42.200 --> 23:43.270
I've got more friends than she does.

23:43.270 --> 23:44.310
Why don't you compare
that strength of mine to hers?

23:44.310 --> 23:46.700
Does the college entrance exam
test popularity?

23:46.700 --> 23:49.030
C-Can having lots of friends
get you into top universities?

23:49.030 --> 23:49.790
Seriously.

23:51.160 --> 23:51.790
Tang Tingting,

23:51.790 --> 23:52.920
I've realized something now.

23:52.920 --> 23:55.780
I-I've realized
your problem isn't your studying.

23:56.030 --> 23:57.880
It's your mindset.

23:58.070 --> 24:00.000
Your attitude is the real problem.

24:00.440 --> 24:02.440
Fine then, you don't have to sign up.

24:02.550 --> 24:03.640
Hand over all those

24:04.030 --> 24:05.200
a-albums of yours.

24:05.200 --> 24:05.790
Mom!

24:07.200 --> 24:09.070
I already told you
I'm not cut out for this.

24:09.070 --> 24:10.550
Are you seriously
going to force me to join?

24:10.550 --> 24:11.880
Fine, I'll go sign up tomorrow.

24:11.880 --> 24:12.920
But if I get eliminated
in the first round,

24:12.920 --> 24:14.790
don't complain that I embarrassed you.

24:14.790 --> 24:15.750
I'll be embarrassed?

24:15.750 --> 24:17.590
Who will really be embarrassed?

24:20.250 --> 24:21.070
Where are you going?

24:21.070 --> 24:22.000
To clear my head.

24:34.880 --> 24:35.480
Tingting.

24:37.200 --> 24:38.480
Why are you all here?

24:41.110 --> 24:42.680
I was just looking for you.

24:43.350 --> 24:45.070
Looking for me? What for?

24:46.160 --> 24:49.360
I'd like to invite you
to join my team for the math contest.

24:51.480 --> 24:52.680
What a coincidence.

24:53.160 --> 24:54.680
I was actually planning to
find two people tomorrow

24:54.680 --> 24:55.790
to sign up with.

24:59.640 --> 25:01.170
But I won't team up with you.

25:03.510 --> 25:04.310
Why?

25:06.200 --> 25:08.530
I'm only entering
to get my mom off my back.

25:08.550 --> 25:10.510
I'll be perfectly happy
getting eliminated in the first round.

25:10.510 --> 25:12.310
How could I
drag the top student down with me?

25:12.310 --> 25:13.680
Are you stupid?

25:14.070 --> 25:15.930
This is such a great opportunity.

25:22.110 --> 25:23.480
Let us talk alone.

25:24.160 --> 25:25.720
It's close to my home anyway.

25:25.720 --> 25:27.180
You guys should head back.

25:28.830 --> 25:30.680
Alright. We'll head back first.

25:35.480 --> 25:36.610
Aren't you leaving?

25:36.880 --> 25:38.200
This is our team's business.

25:38.200 --> 25:39.460
Of course I'm staying.

25:40.160 --> 25:40.960
Alright.

25:41.110 --> 25:42.200
Come on. Let's go.

25:46.030 --> 25:47.790
You guys are really something,

25:47.790 --> 25:48.960
asking me to be your teammate.

25:48.960 --> 25:50.400
You really couldn't find anyone else, huh?

25:50.400 --> 25:51.110
Yes.

25:54.980 --> 25:57.070
Registration is closing soon.

25:57.070 --> 25:58.680
Finding two teammates at the last minute

25:58.680 --> 25:59.680
would be hard for you too, right?

25:59.680 --> 26:00.830
I'm not aiming for any prizes.

26:00.830 --> 26:02.490
I'll just find any two people.

26:03.000 --> 26:06.600
Who's going to join you just to get
knocked out in the first round?

26:06.880 --> 26:09.790
If you pick me,
you'll be eliminated in the first round.

26:09.790 --> 26:10.680
Don't make things harder on yourselves.

26:10.680 --> 26:12.480
You'd better find someone else.

26:15.550 --> 26:17.080
Have you ever thought about

26:17.200 --> 26:19.930
getting first place
to get your mom off your back?

26:20.240 --> 26:21.030
Me?

26:24.110 --> 26:25.350
Since you're signing up anyway,

26:25.350 --> 26:26.550
wouldn't it be a shame

26:26.790 --> 26:28.850
to get eliminated in the first round?

26:30.350 --> 26:31.790
So what am I supposed to do?

26:31.790 --> 26:33.310
That's the best I can do.

26:34.350 --> 26:35.880
Of course, you wouldn't pull it off alone.

26:35.880 --> 26:37.480
But if you join Lin Zhixia's team,

26:37.480 --> 26:38.240
winning first place

26:38.240 --> 26:39.840
isn't entirely impossible.

26:41.070 --> 26:41.790
Right?

26:44.830 --> 26:45.720
Yes.

26:47.550 --> 26:49.680
There's still some time
before the preliminary round.

26:49.680 --> 26:52.070
I can make
an intensive study plan for you.

26:52.090 --> 26:53.510
An intensive study plan?

26:54.510 --> 26:56.640
Isn't that exactly what broke Duan Qiyan?

26:56.640 --> 26:59.680
Just because he couldn't handle it
doesn't mean you can't.

26:59.680 --> 27:01.200
He likes to have fun,

27:01.330 --> 27:03.200
but his grades are still pretty good.

27:03.200 --> 27:04.200
His old nickname

27:04.230 --> 27:06.160
was the "King of
the Affiliated Elementary School."

27:06.160 --> 27:07.830
You earned your place

27:07.850 --> 27:09.400
in the experimental class too.

27:09.400 --> 27:10.930
Don't sell yourself short.

27:16.160 --> 27:17.160
Imagine

27:18.030 --> 27:20.160
what will happen if you get first place

27:20.590 --> 27:21.680
in the contest.

27:24.270 --> 27:27.400
If I get first place...

27:29.640 --> 27:32.400
my mom will probably
buy me the latest phone

27:32.960 --> 27:35.000
and treat me to a big meal.

27:35.960 --> 27:38.720
Maybe she'll even stop nagging me
about idol-chasing.

27:38.720 --> 27:39.750
Leave it to me.

27:40.160 --> 27:43.220
I'll do everything I can
to lead the team to first place.

27:46.720 --> 27:47.510
So?

27:47.830 --> 27:50.790
Are you willing to join our team?

27:52.790 --> 27:55.680
You really want me as your teammate?

27:58.240 --> 27:59.920
I was so mean to you before,

28:00.160 --> 28:02.760
and I even gave you
that nickname, "Immortal."

28:03.130 --> 28:04.880
You don't mind?

28:07.400 --> 28:08.930
Lots of people call me that.

28:09.110 --> 28:10.030
I'm used to it.

28:12.960 --> 28:14.400
Then let me make one thing clear first.

28:14.400 --> 28:15.720
I'm really not good at math.

28:15.720 --> 28:17.310
If I mess up, you can't blame me.

28:17.310 --> 28:18.240
Enough talking.

28:18.510 --> 28:19.440
Since you've joined us,

28:19.440 --> 28:20.440
commit to it.

28:20.640 --> 28:23.240
Aiming for first place
in the entire province.

28:23.400 --> 28:24.260
What do you say?

28:29.350 --> 28:30.350
My two teammates?

28:33.030 --> 28:33.920
Deal.

28:36.030 --> 28:36.790
Deal.

28:37.200 --> 28:37.960
Deal.

29:13.480 --> 29:15.720
This is a geometric sequence
where we're solving for the common ratio q.

29:15.720 --> 29:18.750
So set point B... This point.

29:20.400 --> 29:23.000
Assume point B equals point A...
Write it down.

29:24.550 --> 29:26.590
A1 plus A2 plus A3...

29:27.440 --> 29:28.240
Then...

29:28.260 --> 29:28.980
Stop.

29:30.030 --> 29:31.960
Do you understand it, Shen Fuxuan?

29:32.270 --> 29:33.250
Yeah.

29:33.510 --> 29:34.590
What's so hard to understand?

29:34.590 --> 29:36.070
She's explained it so many times already.

29:36.070 --> 29:37.240
I know.

29:37.240 --> 29:38.900
But I still don't quite get it.

29:39.030 --> 29:41.560
That's okay.
We can go over it a few more times.

29:43.270 --> 29:45.470
How about this? We can study at my place.

29:45.750 --> 29:47.720
We can talk as loudly as we want there.

29:47.720 --> 29:49.450
And maybe when my mom sees

29:49.480 --> 29:50.880
how hard I'm studying,

29:50.880 --> 29:51.640
she'll get so happy

29:51.640 --> 29:54.100
that she'll give me back
my precious albums.

29:54.480 --> 29:55.270
Please.

29:55.270 --> 29:57.470
I haven't listened to his songs in ages.

29:57.880 --> 29:59.200
All right. Let's gather our stuff.

29:59.200 --> 29:59.830
Okay.

30:01.550 --> 30:03.270
Then let me finish this problem.
Two minutes.

30:03.270 --> 30:03.850
Okay.

30:04.590 --> 30:05.550
We'll wait for you at the door.

30:05.550 --> 30:06.240
Okay.

30:14.790 --> 30:17.510
Tang Tingting's riding
Lin Zhixia's coattails into the contest—

30:17.510 --> 30:18.640
she's pretty lucky.

30:20.640 --> 30:22.840
Tang Tingting's dead last in the class.

30:23.000 --> 30:25.160
Shen Fuxuan is okay, though.

30:26.310 --> 30:27.310
But no matter how strong Lin Zhixia is,

30:27.310 --> 30:29.110
she can't carry a hopeless team.

30:30.880 --> 30:31.960
You have a point.

30:33.350 --> 30:34.680
I should study hard too.

30:50.160 --> 30:51.090
Need something?

30:54.270 --> 30:58.130
Sounds like you all have some
strong opinions about what makes a team.

30:58.440 --> 30:59.700
I'd really like to know

31:00.310 --> 31:02.240
what kind of results a deserter...

31:02.830 --> 31:04.290
a perennial runner-up...

31:06.640 --> 31:08.270
and a measly seventh place

31:09.510 --> 31:11.310
can possibly achieve together.

31:20.160 --> 31:21.110
Jeez.

31:22.750 --> 31:24.640
Aren't our grudges settled?

31:24.640 --> 31:26.370
Why does he still talk that way?

31:26.880 --> 31:28.140
That guy, Shen Fuxuan,

31:28.240 --> 31:29.590
has such a sharp tongue,

31:29.590 --> 31:31.190
he might cut himself with it.

31:34.720 --> 31:38.380
Lin Zhixia, how are you still studying
while just standing there?

31:38.830 --> 31:41.650
There's actually a much simpler way
to solve this problem.

31:41.650 --> 31:42.310
Hold on.

31:42.510 --> 31:44.440
Let me take a break. I'm exhausted.

31:44.590 --> 31:45.920
Then look at it again
when we get to your place.

31:45.920 --> 31:47.110
I'm going to find Jiang Yubai.

31:47.110 --> 31:48.970
He asked me about it during class.

31:49.160 --> 31:51.880
Lin Zhixia, they're our competitors.

31:52.750 --> 31:53.590
I know.

31:53.750 --> 31:55.640
But Jiang Yubai is also my good friend.

31:55.640 --> 31:56.400
Don't worry.

31:56.400 --> 31:57.160
They won't use

31:57.160 --> 32:00.020
the exact same problems
during the actual contest.

32:02.960 --> 32:03.750
Jiang Yubai,

32:04.480 --> 32:06.610
you saw how Shen Fuxuan acted just now.

32:06.790 --> 32:08.520
Do you know where you stand now?

32:11.350 --> 32:12.410
I've always known.

32:13.510 --> 32:14.070
Good.

32:14.550 --> 32:15.720
Then our team's goal

32:15.920 --> 32:17.250
is to defeat Lin Zhixia.

32:17.830 --> 32:21.830
And I want to beat them so thoroughly
they have no choice but to accept it.

32:22.160 --> 32:23.020
Same goal here.

32:24.030 --> 32:26.440
I feel like you two are fired up now.

32:26.440 --> 32:27.640
So motivated.

32:29.550 --> 32:30.150
Oh, right.

32:30.270 --> 32:31.030
Jiang Yubai,

32:31.590 --> 32:33.320
you and Lin Zhixia are so close.

32:33.680 --> 32:34.480
If

32:34.480 --> 32:35.830
we beat them,

32:36.000 --> 32:38.060
what will happen to your friendship?

32:40.590 --> 32:42.720
I've always wanted to beat Lin Zhixia.

32:43.880 --> 32:46.420
This contest is our best chance.

32:47.880 --> 32:49.610
Right now, I don't see a friend—

32:49.750 --> 32:50.590
I see my rival.

33:12.350 --> 33:14.480
I've always wanted to beat Lin Zhixia.

33:15.070 --> 33:17.440
This contest is our best chance.

33:18.070 --> 33:19.800
Right now, I don't see a friend—

33:20.000 --> 33:20.880
I see my rival.

34:08.280 --> 34:08.940
Lin Zhixia.

34:09.920 --> 34:10.480
Morning.

34:11.070 --> 34:11.760
Morning.

34:18.460 --> 34:20.989
Let's look at
this original contest problem.

34:21.570 --> 34:22.920
An insulated container is divided

34:22.920 --> 34:25.280
by a partition
into a gas chamber and a vacuum.

34:25.280 --> 34:27.070
The partition is removed,
allowing the gas to expand freely.

34:27.070 --> 34:29.880
Lin Zhixia, could you explain

34:29.920 --> 34:32.050
the problem the teacher just covered?

34:32.590 --> 34:33.400
Sorry.

34:33.710 --> 34:36.170
I wasn't listening to
what the teacher was saying.

34:36.170 --> 34:38.770
As the molecules spread farther apart,
their potential energy increases,

34:38.770 --> 34:40.010
their kinetic energy decreases,

34:40.010 --> 34:41.540
and the temperature drops.

34:42.010 --> 34:44.780
Don't simply apply the ideal gas model
from the textbook.

34:44.780 --> 34:45.670
This is a key testing point.

34:45.670 --> 34:46.800
Pay attention to it.

34:59.150 --> 35:00.510
Free activity time's over.

35:00.510 --> 35:01.840
Everyone, gather here.

35:08.710 --> 35:10.110
Before class ends today,

35:10.280 --> 35:12.960
let's have a fun team obstacle course—

35:13.230 --> 35:14.560
the three-legged race.

35:15.000 --> 35:17.590
It'll help develop your coordination

35:17.590 --> 35:18.670
and teamwork.

35:18.710 --> 35:20.590
Now pair up freely.

35:20.960 --> 35:22.110
Find yourselves a partner.

35:22.110 --> 35:24.320
But I must emphasize one rule:

35:24.510 --> 35:26.800
each team must consist of

35:26.800 --> 35:28.070
one boy and one girl.

35:30.920 --> 35:31.510
Okay.

35:31.670 --> 35:32.930
Go find your partners.

35:34.440 --> 35:35.440
Who should we ask?

35:43.710 --> 35:46.150
Lin Zhixia, let's team up.

35:47.230 --> 35:47.920
Okay.

35:50.030 --> 35:50.800
I...

35:51.230 --> 35:52.030
Jiang Yubai.

35:53.960 --> 35:54.840
Let's team up.

35:55.230 --> 35:55.760
Let's go.

35:59.420 --> 36:00.940
Let's pair up.

36:01.300 --> 36:02.160
Let's go, Chun.

36:03.900 --> 36:05.230
Aren't I your teammate?

36:06.050 --> 36:07.650
Am I invisible or something?

36:15.400 --> 36:16.600
Wanna team up with me?

37:36.170 --> 37:36.820
Water.

37:45.650 --> 37:46.450
What's wrong?

37:47.940 --> 37:49.800
You seem to have a lot on your mind.

37:55.150 --> 37:56.610
I heard you said yesterday

37:56.990 --> 37:58.170
that from now on,

37:58.170 --> 38:00.170
we're only opponents, not friends.

38:00.610 --> 38:02.010
Because of this contest,

38:02.340 --> 38:04.140
are we not even friends anymore?

38:11.760 --> 38:14.160
Actually, before we formed teams that day,

38:14.310 --> 38:15.500
Mr. Kong told me

38:16.300 --> 38:19.650
that you already have what it takes
to skip ahead and go to university early,

38:19.650 --> 38:20.980
but I don't.

38:23.050 --> 38:25.380
Those words really struck a chord with me.

38:27.470 --> 38:28.530
This contest

38:29.170 --> 38:31.370
is a great opportunity to prove myself.

38:31.500 --> 38:33.610
That's why, when we were choosing teams,

38:33.610 --> 38:36.140
I deliberately avoided
partnering with you.

38:38.660 --> 38:40.420
I want to give it everything I've got

38:40.420 --> 38:41.820
and compete against you

38:41.900 --> 38:43.760
without any distractions.

38:44.690 --> 38:47.010
I also want to see,
after working so hard for so long,

38:47.010 --> 38:49.270
just how big
the gap between us really is.

38:50.100 --> 38:53.170
Is this contest
really that important to you?

38:53.970 --> 38:54.690
Yes.

38:56.330 --> 38:57.260
Very important.

39:01.800 --> 39:03.400
This was yet another setback

39:03.780 --> 39:05.130
in my social life.

39:07.390 --> 39:09.190
I suddenly find myself doubting

39:10.070 --> 39:13.200
whether all those promises
we made to work hard together

39:13.230 --> 39:15.030
were just my personal illusion.

39:16.820 --> 39:19.420
It turns out Jiang Yubai's true pride

39:20.590 --> 39:22.990
lies in having a rival
worthy of defeating.

39:24.530 --> 39:25.420
And "friend"

39:27.230 --> 39:29.380
was nothing more than a label
I gave myself out of wishful thinking.
